From: Sunil Dora <sunilkumar.dora@windriver.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rustc_codegen_llvm: skip removed AMX-TF32 mapping with LLVM 23
Origin: vendor, https://git.openembedded.org/openembedded-core/commit/?id=99548382539f2e9b7fb9ba182f9e0f6707d4f360
Forwarded: not-needed

Peios builds Rust 1.98 against its system LLVM 23 rather than Rust's bundled
LLVM, so rustc must not ask LLVM 23 for a feature it no longer has. Upstream
Rust dropped the mapping itself after 1.98
(https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/159310), so this 1.98-only fix has
nothing to forward.

LLVM removed AMX-TF32 in https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/207673.
Keep the existing Rust mapping with earlier LLVM versions, but omit this
one removed backend feature on LLVM 23 and later. The standard target
feature query otherwise aborts before compiling any program.

This is the two-line OpenEmbedded compatibility fix, with local provenance
headers. It does not change generic unknown-feature handling or claim
hardware support for an explicitly requested unstable feature.

--- a/compiler/rustc_codegen_llvm/src/llvm_util.rs
+++ b/compiler/rustc_codegen_llvm/src/llvm_util.rs
@@ -286,6 +286,8 @@
                     s,
                     smallvec![TargetFeatureFoldStrength::EnableOnly("evex512")],
                 )),
+                // AMX-TF32 was removed from LLVM 23
+                "amx-tf32" if major >= 23 => None,
                 "avx10.1" if major < 22 => Some(LLVMFeature::new("avx10.1-512")),
                 "avx10.2" if major < 22 => Some(LLVMFeature::new("avx10.2-512")),
                 "apxf" => Some(LLVMFeature::with_dependencies(
